	(text "CANary-PWR rev 1.0 -- supercapacitor UPS and always-on supervisor for the Pi 5 + CANary HAT"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 25.4 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "b492cc35-becb-474a-a0ed-09e640b2ec62")
	)
	(text "Stack: NVMe base / Pi 5 / CANary-PWR / CANary HAT (rev 2.1 and later). PWR plugs directly on the Pi; the HAT plugs on PWR's stacking header.\nPower path: OBD 12 V -> reverse block + TVS -> charger switch (TPS1HB35) -> LTC3350 input ideal diode -> +12V_BUS (backed up by the cap bank)\n            +12V_BUS -> LM61460 5.1 V -> INA226 shunt -> LM74700 ideal diode -> Pi header pins 2/4 (Power HAT+ style, no USB-C)\n            +12V_BUS -> TPS1HB35 -> HAT out terminal -> jumper to the HAT's J2\nEvery switch defaults ON: a dead or resetting supervisor degrades to an always-on Pi, never a dark rig.\nSupervisor <-> Pi: I2C1 through a Pi-powered TCA4307, GPIO6 = power fail (HIGH = OK), GPIO27 = MCU BOOT0, GPIO24 = MCU reset, Pi 3V3 sense.\nNets are connected by labels on this first pass; global labels cross sheets."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 45.72 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "96a646cb-f806-4512-ad14-9c16cf391746")
	)
